# `.copy` is this repo's suffix for checked-in generator output, kept for build
# machines that lack the generator -- today Lemon / re2c under as/src/exp. The
# rules are unscoped because the suffix, not the directory, is what means
# "generated". The reviewable artifact is the .re / .y it comes from.
#
# Marked generated so review tools de-emphasise them, and `-diff` so git reports
# a one-line "differ" instead of thousands of lines nobody reads. Both generators
# now run on a bare filename inside GEN_DIR, so their output is byte-identical
# from any directory -- staleness is binary, and "differ" is the whole answer.
# `git diff --text` when the hunks are actually wanted.
*.copy linguist-generated=true
*.copy -diff
